From c36d414628a29c9c04fbfc2e6d0d790f7ceb927b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabe Ochoa <urgentcactus@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 06:54:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] Virtual list: bounded window with configurable overscan,
 keyed rows

virtual_list_window bounds the reach toward a distant easing target around
the actual viewport, so a scrollbar drag never drops the rows on screen
(CP-006). VirtualListOptions sets row and pixel overscan; VirtualListMetrics
accepts precomputed logical row heights so one set of extents drives both the
window and the caller's geometry. The shortest row is cached instead of
rescanned every build.

keyed_virtual_list keeps the item at the top of the viewport (or its nearest
survivor) in place when the sequence changes, keeps the anchor through an
empty sequence, and moves focus to whichever pooled row now draws the
focused item.
