From 74916dceba88fee444b74907d8968acac6d2860d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabe Ochoa <urgentcactus@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 06:59:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] Scroll: logical item anchors resolved after layout
 readiness

request_scroll_anchor/resolve_scroll_anchor keep an item named by an
app-owned key at a fraction of the unoccluded viewport band. The request
waits for the matching content generation and a measured viewport, resolves
once to Applied, Unavailable (key gone or content replaced) or Cancelled, and
writes offset, target and easing in one jump_to_y. No frame-count retries.

HasScrollView::user_scroll_serial is bumped by wheel input and scrollbar
drags, so cancellation follows real user input rather than any change to
scroll_target, which clamping and virtual lists also make.
