--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -30,6 +30,12 @@ Started partway through the project's life, so it does not go all the way back.
 - **Menu shortcuts sit one pad in from the panel edge** — they were flush, clipping the last glyph in half.
 
 ### New APIs
+- **Focus-scoped shortcut routing** (`ui/shortcut_routing.h`). `ShortcutRouter::dispatch` offers a mapped action or a raw chord to the focused control, then each containing `ShortcutScope`, then the app callback `router.app`. Native menus and tests call that same callback. One taker per frame: a taken action is cleared from `UIContext`, so a widget polling `pressed()` later cannot run it again, and a second dispatch reports `Repeated`. Text fields keep typing and caret keys, Option+Left included. Exclusive scopes contain dialogs. A gated focus swallows input. Register `RouteShortcuts<Action>` after `BeginUIContextManager`.
+- **Focus return by logical identity** (`ui/focus_return.h`). Attach `FocusKey{scope, control}` to controls and call `FocusReturnStack::opened/closed/resolve` around an overlay. Focus returns to the rebuilt control, under whatever entity id it has now, only if its scope still exists and it can take focus. Otherwise it goes to the fallback you named. Nested overlays and outside-click dismissal are handled. `Modal` and `menu` still keep their raw-id restore; this is opt-in.
+- **Logical scroll anchors** (`ui/scroll_item_anchor.h`). `request_scroll_anchor(view, {key, within, fraction, insets, generation})` waits for your content generation and a measured viewport, then applies once. The result is `Applied`, `Unavailable` or `Cancelled`; no frame-count retries. `HasScrollView::user_scroll_serial` and `jump_to_y()` are new; wheel input and scrollbar drags bump the serial.
+- **`VirtualListOptions` / `virtual_list_window` / `VirtualListMetrics`.** Overscan in rows or pixels, and accepts precomputed logical row heights. The window is now bounded around the actual viewport: a scrollbar drag used to favour the far target and could build a window that omitted the rows on screen. The shortest row is cached instead of rescanned per build. Default overscan is unchanged.
+- **`keyed_virtual_list(ctx, ep, count, revision, key_of, height_of, render_row)`** keeps the top item (or its nearest survivor) and keyboard focus with their items when the sequence changes. A change re-measures every row.
+- **Read-only source selection** (`ui/source_selection.h`). Selection over a `TextSource` (line_count/line) by `(line, byte)`, so it survives a virtualized viewport. It provides tab and soft-wrap display mapping, hit-testing and highlight extents, keyboard movement with identifier words, `select_word`/`select_line`, `edge_autoscroll`, and `copy_text`, which keeps tabs, CRLF and UTF-8 byte-exact and refuses output over a limit.
 - **`polyline::draw_dashed(pts, thickness, color, dash, gap, phase)`** (`polyline.h`) draws a patterned run. `draw_line_ex` was solid-only, so a dashed cable, marquee or tick run had to be hand-rolled. Arc length accumulates across vertices, so a dash straddling a corner stays one dash, and `phase` is what animates it.
 - **`polyline::resample_by_arclength(pts, step)`** returns evenly spaced points. A bezier sampler walks uniformly in `t`, which is not uniform in screen distance, so anything spaced along the result bunches where the curve is tight.
 - **`draw_line_ex` is recorded by capture**, so a test can assert on a dashed pattern. The `none` backend used to log `@notimplemented` and draw nothing.
